arguments.body:
Q2 2027 Helio Start paid-test proposal — working draft

Decisions that remain unapproved

| Decision | Status | Boundary preserved in this draft |
|---|---|---|
| Whether to run paid traffic or launch the test | UNAPPROVED | Priya authorized proposal development only; no paid traffic, launch, or launch authorization is approved. |
| Budget or spend authorization | UNAPPROVED | No budget is approved. The proposed test has one hard operating close at the earlier of $8,000 in paid-source spend or 25 paid-source admissions; that close is not a budget, spend authorization, or entitlement. |
| Test scale, traffic, audience, channel, or geography | UNAPPROVED | This draft presents one precisely bounded test shape only: one paid-source cohort and one paid batch, closed at the earlier-of-$8,000-or-25-admissions condition. It presents no alternative budget, scale, traffic, audience, channel, or geography options. |
| Launch timing or start date | UNAPPROVED | No start date, operating window, or timing commitment is set. |
| Paid-source definition and reconciliation sources | UNAPPROVED | Owners must approve the paid-source/campaign taxonomy, source-of-truth systems, join keys, and reconciliation method before any launch decision. |
| Admission ownership and close monitoring | UNAPPROVED | The admission counter owner and monitoring method remain to be assigned and approved. |
| Pipeline treatment or pipeline target | UNAPPROVED | This draft proposes no pipeline treatment, target, or reporting change. |
| Forecast credit or forecast assumption | UNAPPROVED | This draft proposes no forecast credit, forecast assumption, or performance credit. |
| Any second paid batch | UNAPPROVED | No second paid batch is authorized or committed. |
| Exceptions, restarts, and later commercial decisions | UNAPPROVED | Any launch, restart, exception, or later commercial decision requires separate approval. |

Status and purpose

Priya authorized development of this proposal. This document is a development draft for review, not an approved launch plan. Proposal development is authorized; execution is not. Nothing here authorizes paid traffic, a budget, a launch, launch timing, pipeline treatment, forecast credit, a pipeline target, or a second paid batch. The measurement design below is an operating and learning view only; it is not acquisition evidence, pipeline evidence, revenue evidence, or forecast evidence.

Paid traffic status

Paid traffic remains off through March 31, 2027. No paid campaign, audience, spend, or traffic activation is implied by this draft.

Precisely bounded test shape

The proposed Q2 paid test is one bounded learning exercise for Helio Start:

- one paid-source cohort;
- one paid batch, with no scale-up path or alternative batch presented here;
- one hard close at the earlier of $8,000 in paid-source spend or 25 paid-source admissions; and
- end-to-end source reconciliation and the operating stop/pause controls below.

This is a single proposed shape, not approval to execute it. It does not set a budget or traffic plan. Any eventual execution would require the unapproved decisions above, complete instrumentation and source reconciliation, and explicit launch authorization. The proposal preserves all existing eligibility, refusal, connector-access, external-authority, lifecycle, instrumentation, and assisted-routing rules.

Measurement-operating shape

The running view is a measurement and operating-control view, not acquisition, pipeline, revenue, or forecast evidence. It must preserve these as separate counts, with their own source, definition, as-of time, and reconciliation status:

- paid-source eligibility-flow starts;
- assisted routes;
- admissions; and
- attribution failures.

Do not collapse these counts into a funnel, conversion claim, acquisition result, pipeline measure, revenue measure, or forecast input. In particular, an eligibility-flow start is not an admission; an assisted route is not an admission; and an attribution failure is not silently assigned to any other count. The running view must retain unresolved, duplicate, missing, and conflicting records as explicit exceptions.

After the view contains at least 10 admissions, it must show the account-level support signal for the admitted cohort as both:

- the number of admitted workspaces exceeding 90 account-level support minutes; and
- the share of admitted workspaces exceeding 90 account-level support minutes.

Show the denominator, cohort definition, measurement window, source, as-of time, and exceptions with those two values. This operational support signal may inform the post-10-admission pause below, but it is not a mature account-level support-effort claim. Do not redefine the denominator or exclude affected accounts to improve the displayed share.

When the paid test closes, freeze the admitted cohort used for reporting. The closed cohort remains fixed after closure: do not add later admissions, remove admitted workspaces, reassign cohort membership, or rewrite the denominator to change a result. Corrections must be versioned and documented as corrections to the fixed cohort, with the original snapshot retained.

Day-7 first integration may appear only as a leading indicator. It must be labeled explicitly as day-7, shown separately from admissions and mature outcomes, and must not be used as paid-active status, refund-adjusted collected cash, account-level support effort, a final test conclusion, acquisition evidence, pipeline evidence, revenue evidence, or forecast evidence.

Operating stop and pause rules

These are operating controls for a future, separately approved test. They are distinct from later day-90 maturity and outcome claims. The running view above does not change these controls or create commercial evidence.

Close conditions: earlier of $8,000 or 25 admissions

The paid test must close at the earlier of:

- $8,000 in paid-source spend; or
- 25 paid-source admissions.

The close is a hard operating stop, not a target, budget approval, scale option, or entitlement. Spend and admissions must be monitored against the close conditions using reconciled source data. No additional paid traffic may be activated after the earlier condition is reached unless a separately approved proposal authorizes a new test. The close condition does not establish a budget, traffic target, pipeline target, or forecast assumption. At closure, freeze the admitted cohort as specified in the measurement-operating shape above.

Unsupported-admission stop

Stop paid acquisition and admission processing immediately if any admission is unsupported by the required eligibility, source, connector-access, external-authority, lifecycle, or other governing evidence. An unsupported admission must not be admitted, routed, or treated as a valid paid-test result. The issue must be documented, the affected record held for review, and the accountable owner notified. Restart requires resolution and explicit approval under the unchanged governing rules.

Routing or instrumentation pause

Pause paid routing and paid-test progression if assisted-routing behavior or required instrumentation is missing, materially delayed, contradictory, or unreliable, including when the failure prevents paid-source attribution from reconciling from eligibility-flow start through admission and assisted routing. The pause applies until event capture, ordering, attribution, and routing-state integrity are restored and verified. During the pause, do not infer missing events, backfill credit without evidence, admit affected records, or continue paid traffic on the assumption that the gap is harmless. Any restart requires owner sign-off and documented verification of the repaired path.

Post-10-admission support pause

Once at least 10 paid-source admissions exist, use the running view to show both the number and share of admitted workspaces exceeding 90 account-level support minutes. If more than 10% of admitted workspaces exceed 90 account-level support minutes, pause additional paid admissions and paid routing. The fixed admitted cohort and the stated denominator remain controlling; do not exclude accounts or redefine the cohort to avoid the threshold. Do not resume until the support-effort issue has an owner, documented diagnosis, corrective action, and verified evidence that the threshold is no longer exceeded. This is an operating pause trigger, not a mature-outcome claim and not a reason to treat incomplete support data as a mature account-level support-effort result. The support calculation and exception list must be retained with the reporting snapshot.

End-to-end paid-source attribution reconciliation

Before any result is accepted, reconcile paid-source attribution end to end, from eligibility-flow start through admission and assisted routing. The reconciliation must establish, for each claimed paid-source record:

- the paid source and campaign/source identifiers;
- the eligibility-flow start event and timestamp;
- the applicable eligibility and refusal outcomes;
- connector-access status and the relevant access evidence;
- any required external-authority evidence and its status;
- admission event, timestamp, and admission identifier;
- lifecycle state and transitions;
- assisted-routing event, timestamp, destination, and outcome, where routing occurs;
- the join keys and event ordering used to connect the record across systems; and
- exclusions, duplicates, missing events, attribution conflicts, and unresolved records.

Reconciliation must be performed before reporting admissions, conversion, collected cash, support effort, or any other paid-test result. Records without defensible end-to-end attribution remain unresolved and cannot be counted as paid-source admissions or credited to the test. The reconciliation output must be retained with an owner, as-of time, and exception log. Attribution failures remain a separate running-view count and cannot be converted into starts, routes, or admissions without evidence.

Later mature-outcome measurement: complete day-90 requirements

These requirements apply to later outcome and maturity claims; they do not replace or soften the operating stop and pause rules above. A complete day-90 review is required for every eligible paid-source account before paid-active status, refund-adjusted collected cash, account-level support effort, or test-level mature conclusions are finalized. Until the complete day-90 window is available and reconciled, these measures are unavailable for mature claims; do not substitute day-7 first integration, admission, a partial support window, bookings, invoices, charges, or any other intermediate signal.

1. Paid-active status

Define and verify whether the account is still paid-active at day 90 using the agreed account-level status source and as-of timestamp. Record cancellations, pauses, failed payments, refunds, and other lifecycle changes. Do not substitute an intermediate activation or admission event for day-90 paid-active status. Day-7 first integration remains only a leading indicator.

2. Refund-adjusted collected cash

Report collected cash through day 90 net of refunds, using the agreed account-level transaction source and explicit treatment of reversals, credits, chargebacks, and partial refunds. Show gross collected cash, refunds and other deductions, and refund-adjusted collected cash, with currency, time window, source, and as-of timestamp. Do not use bookings, invoices issued, or unadjusted charges as a substitute. No refund-adjusted collected-cash mature claim is available before the complete day-90 window.

3. Account-level support effort

Measure support effort at the account level through day 90 using the agreed definition and source data. Include the effort components in scope, account linkage, time window, denominator, and treatment of escalations or shared work. Report both the account-level observations and the aggregate rate used for the post-10-admission pause. The post-10-admission running support signal is an operating control only; it does not establish a mature account-level support-effort claim before the complete day-90 window. Missing or ambiguous account linkage must be shown as an exception rather than silently dropped.

The day-90 review is incomplete if any of these three requirements is missing, not reconciled, lacks an owner/as-of time, or depends on unsupported inference. Incomplete day-90 data cannot establish paid-active status, refund-adjusted collected cash, support-effort compliance, or a final mature test conclusion. No mature-outcome claim should be used to override an operating stop or pause. The fixed admitted cohort remains fixed after closure, including for any later day-90 review.

Rules that remain unchanged

This proposal does not change or weaken any existing:

- eligibility rules;
- refusal rules;
- connector-access requirements;
- external-authority requirements;
- lifecycle rules or state transitions;
- instrumentation requirements or event definitions; or
- assisted-routing rules, permissions, destinations, or evidence requirements.

Existing refusal, access, authority, lifecycle, instrumentation, and routing decisions remain controlling. Paid-source attribution cannot override them, and a marketing source cannot create eligibility or authority that is otherwise absent. The measurement-operating shape does not create acquisition, pipeline, revenue, or forecast evidence.

Owner inputs required

Owners must provide and approve, before any launch decision:

- the paid-source and campaign taxonomy, source-of-truth systems, join keys, and reconciliation owner;
- the definitions and owners for separate counts of paid-source eligibility-flow starts, assisted routes, admissions, and attribution failures;
- the eligibility, refusal, connector-access, external-authority, lifecycle, instrumentation, and assisted-routing owners;
- the admission counter owner and close-condition monitoring method;
- the unsupported-admission detection and escalation owner;
